/-
# Generators of the augmentation ideal of a free product (Kourovka Notebook Problem 5.10)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 5.10 (K. W. Gruenberg): let E = H * K and
denote the augmentation ideals of E, H, K by e, h, k; if I is a right ideal of ZE, let d_E(I) be the
minimum number of generators of I as a right ideal. Assuming H and K finitely generated, is d_E(e) =
d_E(hE) + d_E(kE)?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Module.SpanRank
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Coprod.Basic
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Finiteness
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.GroupRingRightIdealShared

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.AugmentationIdealGeneratorsFreeProductKourovka5Problem10Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 5.10 (K. W.
Gruenberg). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700294 (`KOU-5.10`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

`E = H * K` is `Monoid.Coprod H K`. Right ideals of the integral group ring `ℤE = MonoidAlgebra ℤ E`
are Mathlib's right submodules `Submodule (ℤE)ᵐᵒᵖ (ℤE)`. The augmentation ideal `e` of `ℤE` is the
right ideal generated by all `g - 1` (as a set, `augmentationIdeal` of the Kourovka 12.22 entry),
and `hE`, `kE` are the right ideals generated by the `h - 1` and `k - 1` with `h ∈ H`, `k ∈ K` (the
augmentation ideal of `ℤH` is spanned by the `h - 1`): the shared
`GroupRingRightIdealShared.augmentationRightIdeal`. `d_E(I)` is Mathlib's `Submodule.spanFinrank`,
the least number of generators of `I` as a right ideal (all these ideals are finitely generated,
since `H` and `K` are).
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.GroupRingRightIdealShared

/-- Kourovka 5.10 (K. W. Gruenberg): for finitely generated groups `H` and `K` and `E = H * K`,
the augmentation ideal `e` of `ℤE` satisfies `d_E(e) = d_E(hE) + d_E(kE)`, where `hE` and `kE`
are the right ideals of `ℤE` generated by the augmentation ideals of `ℤH` and `ℤK` and `d_E` is
the least number of generators of a right ideal of `ℤE` (Mathlib's `Submodule.spanFinrank`). -/
def augmentationIdealRankAdditive : Prop :=
  ∀ (H K : Type) [Group H] [Group K] [Group.FG H] [Group.FG K],
    (augmentationRightIdeal (Set.univ : Set (Monoid.Coprod H K))).spanFinrank =
      (augmentationRightIdeal
          (Set.range (Monoid.Coprod.inl : H →* Monoid.Coprod H K))).spanFinrank +
        (augmentationRightIdeal
          (Set.range (Monoid.Coprod.inr : K →* Monoid.Coprod H K))).spanFinrank

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 5.10 "Not always" (P. A. Linnell, unpublished), with
the example of Gruenberg's letter of 27 July 1995: for `H` elementary abelian of order `4` and `K`
elementary abelian of order `9`, `d_E(e) = 3` while `d_E(hE) = d_E(kE) = 2`. Source: E. I. Khukhro
and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue,
arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 5.10 (K. W. Gruenberg); resolution:
P. A. Linnell, unpublished; K. W. Gruenberg, letter of 27 July 1995, Kourovka Archive, Problem 5.10:
Not always (Linnell); a simple example: H elementary abelian of order 4, K elementary abelian of
order 9, where d_E(e) = 3 although d_E(hE) = d_E(kE) = 2 (Gruenberg),
https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted augmentationIdealRankAdditive_refuted : ¬ augmentationIdealRankAdditive

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.AugmentationIdealGeneratorsFreeProductKourovka5Problem10Wanted
